    "project_template_level_name": "aif-y2-natural-language-processing-lesson13-choice1-2026 + template",
    "long_instructions": "Now that `model` is filled in, you can use it to generate new text.\r\n\r\nThe `generate` function starts from one token and keeps choosing a next token until the sentence ends.\r\n\r\nFor example, starting from \"The\", the model might build a sentence like this:\r\n\r\n```\r\n[\"The\"]\r\n[\"The\", \"proof\"]\r\n[\"The\", \"proof\", \"is\"]\r\n[\"The\", \"proof\", \"is\", \"always\"]\r\n[\"The\", \"proof\", \"is\", \"always\", \"right\"]\r\n[\"The\", \"proof\", \"is\", \"always\", \"right\", \".\"]\r\n```\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n- Complete the `generate` function.\r\n  - Create a list to hold the generated tokens. Make it hold `start`—the current token.\r\n  - While a sentence is not yet complete:\r\n      - Randomly choose the next token from the current token’s list in `model`.\r\n      - Append that token to your list of tokens, and make it the current token.\r\n  - When a sentence is complete, return your list of tokens.\r\n- Answer the question under **Step 4: Build Your Model** in your Project Planning Guide.\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\nA `while` loop repeats until its condition is no longer true.\r\n\r\n```\r\nwhile token != \".\":\r\n  ...\r\n```\r\n\r\n`random.choice` picks a random item from a list.\r\n\r\n```\r\ntoken = random.choice(model[token])\r\n```",
    "bubble_choice_description": "A collection of short sayings that express some truth.",
